(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and explain the fundamental differential relations connecting position s\(t\), velocity v\(t\), and acceleration a\(t\) in rectilinear kinematics of particles.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Rectilinear Kinematics Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   Rectilinear motion refers to the one-dimensional motion of a particle along a straight) Tj
T*
(   geometric path.) Tj
T*
(   - Position Displacement: s\(t\) defines the directed algebraic distance from a fixed reference) Tj
T*
(   origin O.) Tj
T*
(   - Instantaneous Velocity: v\(t\) is defined as the first time derivative of position: v = ds/dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Instantaneous Acceleration: a\(t\) is defined as the time rate of change of velocity: a = dv/dt) Tj
T*
(   = d^2s/dt^2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Elimination of Time Variable \(v-s-a Relation\):) Tj
T*
(   Applying the chain rule of differential calculus:) Tj
T*
(   a = dv/dt = \(dv/ds\) * \(ds/dt\) = v * \(dv/ds\).) Tj
T*
(   Rearranging into differential form: a ds = v dv.) Tj
T*
(   This differential relationship is indispensable when acceleration is expressed as an explicit) Tj
T*
(   function of position a = f\(s\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Three General Integration Regimes:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) a = f\(t\): v\(t\) = v0 + Integral_0^t f\(tau\) dtau; s\(t\) = s0 + Integral_0^t v\(tau\) dtau.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) a = f\(v\): dt = dv / f\(v\) => t = Integral_v0^v dv / f\(v\); ds = v dv / f\(v\) => s =) Tj
T*
(   Integral_v0^v v dv / f\(v\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) a = f\(s\): Integral_s0^s f\(s\) ds = Integral_v0^v v dv = 0.5 * \(v^2 - v0^2\) => v\(s\) = sqrt\() Tj
T*
(   v0^2 + 2 * Integral_s0^s f\(s\) ds \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the three classical kinematic equations of motion for a particle travelling in a straight line with constant uniform acceleration 'a'.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Velocity-Time Equation \(v = u + a*t\):) Tj
T*
(   By definition: a = dv/dt = constant.) Tj
T*
(   Separating variables: dv = a dt.) Tj
T*
(   Integrating between initial state \(t = 0, v = u\) and final state \(t, v\):) Tj
T*
(   Integral_u^v dv = a * Integral_0^t dt => [v]_u^v = a * [t]_0^t => v - u = a*t => v = u + a*t.) Tj
T*
(   \(Equation 1\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Position-Time Equation \(s = u*t + 0.5*a*t^2\):) Tj
T*
(   By definition: v = ds/dt => ds = v dt.) Tj
T*
(   Substituting Equation 1: ds = \(u + a*t\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   Integrating between \(t = 0, s = 0\) and \(t, s\):) Tj
T*
(   Integral_0^s ds = Integral_0^t \(u + a*t\) dt => s = u*t + 0.5*a*t^2. \(Equation 2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Velocity-Displacement Equation \(v^2 = u^2 + 2*a*s\):) Tj
T*
(   From the chain rule relation: a ds = v dv.) Tj
T*
(   With a = constant: a * Integral_0^s ds = Integral_u^v v dv.) Tj
T*
(   a * s = 0.5 * [v^2]_u^v = 0.5 * \(v^2 - u^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Multiplying both sides by 2 and rearranging:) Tj
T*
(   v^2 - u^2 = 2*a*s => v^2 = u^2 + 2*a*s. \(Equation 3\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
