BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A pile-driving hammer falls freely under gravity from rest at height h = 5.0 m onto a precast concrete pile foundation. Calculate: \(1\) Impact velocity v_impact, \(2\) If the pile penetrates Delta s = 0.08 m into soil before the hammer stops, compute the average deceleration and the soil resistance force assuming hammer mass m = 800 kg \(g = 9.81 m/s^2\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Free Fall Phase Kinematics:) Tj
T*
(   Initial state: u = 0, a = + g = 9.81 m/s^2, fall distance h = 5.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   v_impact^2 = u^2 + 2*g*h = 0 + 2 * 9.81 * 5.0 = 98.10 \(m/s\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   v_impact = sqrt\(98.10\) = 9.9045 m/s =~ 9.90 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Penetration Phase Deceleration:) Tj
T*
(   During penetration: initial velocity u_p = 9.9045 m/s, final velocity v_p = 0, penetration) Tj
T*
(   distance s_p = 0.08 m.) Tj
T*
(   v_p^2 = u_p^2 + 2*a_avg*s_p => 0 = 98.10 + 2 * a_avg * 0.08 => 0.16 * a_avg = - 98.10.) Tj
T*
(   a_avg = - 98.10 / 0.16 = - 613.125 m/s^2 \(downward deceleration\).) Tj
T*
(   Deceleration magnitude = 613.13 m/s^2 =~ 62.5 g.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Soil Resistance Force Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   By Newton's Second Law applied to the hammer during penetration:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma F_y = m * a => W - R_soil = m * a_avg \(taking downward positive\).) Tj
T*
(   m*g - R_soil = m * \(- 613.125\) => R_soil = m * \(g + 613.125\).) Tj
T*
(   R_soil = 800 * \(9.81 + 613.125\) = 800 * 622.935 = 498,348 N = 498.35 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Alternative Verification via Work-Energy Principle:) Tj
T*
(   Total work done by gravity + soil resistance = Delta KE = 0.) Tj
T*
(   W * \(h + s_p\) - R_soil * s_p = 0 => R_soil = m*g * \(h + s_p\) / s_p.) Tj
T*
(   R_soil = 800 * 9.81 * \(5.0 + 0.08\) / 0.08 = 7848 * 5.08 / 0.08 = 498,348 N = 498.35 kN.) Tj
T*
(   \(Identical match!\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
