BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the formulation of Curvilinear Motion in Normal-Tangential \(n-t\) coordinates. Derive expressions for tangential and normal acceleration components and state the physical interpretation of each.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Coordinate System Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   Let a particle travel along an arbitrary smooth planar path s\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Unit Tangent Vector u_t: Directed tangentially along the path in the direction of increasing) Tj
T*
(   arc length s.) Tj
T*
(   - Unit Principal Normal Vector u_n: Directed perpendicular to u_t, pointing inward toward the) Tj
T*
(   center of curvature C.) Tj
T*
(   - Velocity Vector: v = v * u_t, where v = ds/dt is the scalar speed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Differentiation of the Velocity Vector:) Tj
T*
(   Acceleration is the time derivative of velocity:) Tj
T*
(   a = dv/dt = d/dt\( v * u_t \) = \(dv/dt\) * u_t + v * \(du_t/dt\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivative of the Unit Tangent Vector du_t/dt:) Tj
T*
(   Consider an infinitesimal displacement ds subtending center angle dtheta at radius of curvature) Tj
T*
(   rho \(ds = rho * dtheta\):) Tj
T*
(   The change in direction is |du_t| = 1 * dtheta = ds / rho.) Tj
T*
(   Directed toward the center of curvature along u_n: du_t = dtheta * u_n = \(ds / rho\) * u_n.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: du_t / dt = \(ds/dt\) / rho * u_n = \(v / rho\) * u_n.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complete Acceleration Vector Components:) Tj
T*
