(   Substituting into the acceleration equation:) Tj
T*
(   a = \(dv/dt\) * u_t + \(v^2 / rho\) * u_n = a_t * u_t + a_n * u_n.) Tj
T*
(   - Tangential Acceleration: a_t = dv/dt = v * \(dv/ds\). Physical meaning: Represents the time) Tj
T*
(   rate of change of the SPEED \(magnitude of velocity\).) Tj
T*
(   - Normal Acceleration: a_n = v^2 / rho. Physical meaning: Represents the time rate of change of) Tj
T*
(   the DIRECTION of velocity \(centripetal acceleration\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total Acceleration Magnitude: a = sqrt\( a_t^2 + a_n^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Direction Angle: phi = atan\( a_n / a_t \).) Tj
