(   [Problem Statement]: A haulage dump truck travels along a circular horizontal haul road of radius rho = 250 m. Starting from rest at t = 0, its speed increases at constant rate a_t = 1.2 m/s^2. Determine: \(1\) Time required to achieve speed v = 18 m/s \(64.8 km/h\), \(2\) The normal acceleration a_n at that instant, \(3\) The total acceleration magnitude and its angle with the road tangent.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Time to Reach Velocity v = 18 m/s:) Tj
T*
(   Since tangential acceleration is constant \(a_t = 1.2 m/s^2\):) Tj
T*
(   v = v0 + a_t * t => 18 = 0 + 1.2 * t => t = 18 / 1.2 = 15.0 seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Normal Acceleration at t = 15 s:) Tj
T*
(   a_n = v^2 / rho = \(18\)^2 / 250 = 324 / 250 = 1.296 m/s^2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Total Acceleration Magnitude:) Tj
T*
(   a = sqrt\( a_t^2 + a_n^2 \) = sqrt\( \(1.2\)^2 + \(1.296\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 1.44 + 1.6796 \) = sqrt\( 3.1196) Tj
T*
(   \) = 1.766 m/s^2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Acceleration Orientation Angle:) Tj
T*
(   Angle phi between acceleration vector a and the tangent vector u_t:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(phi\) = a_n / a_t = 1.296 / 1.200 = 1.080 => phi = atan\(1.080\) = 47.20 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion: Time t = 15.0 s; Normal acceleration a_n = 1.30 m/s^2; Total acceleration a = 1.77) Tj
T*
(   m/s^2 at 47.2 deg inward from the road tangent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the complete kinematic expressions for Projectile Motion in a vertical plane: \(1\) Equation of trajectory, \(2\) Time of flight T, \(3\) Maximum height H, \(4\) Horizontal range R.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Coordinate System & Equations of Motion:) Tj
T*
(   Origin at launch point \(x0 = 0, y0 = 0\). Launch speed u at angle theta to horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   Horizontal motion \(ax = 0\): vx\(t\) = u*cos\(theta\); x\(t\) = u*cos\(theta\)*t. \(Eq 1\)) Tj
T*
(   Vertical motion \(ay = - g\): vy\(t\) = u*sin\(theta\) - g*t; y\(t\) = u*sin\(theta\)*t - 0.5*g*t^2. \(Eq) Tj
T*
(   2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Equation of Trajectory:) Tj
T*
(   From Eq 1: t = x / \(u*cos\(theta\)\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute into Eq 2: y = u*sin\(theta\) * [x / \(u*cos\(theta\)\)] - 0.5*g * [x / \(u*cos\(theta\)\)]^2.) Tj
T*
(   y\(x\) = x * tan\(theta\) - [ g / \(2 * u^2 * cos^2\(theta\)\) ] * x^2.) Tj
T*
(   This is the standard equation of a downward-opening parabola.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Time of Flight \(T\):) Tj
T*
(   For landing on level ground, y\(T\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   0 = T * [ u*sin\(theta\) - 0.5*g*T ] => T = \(2 * u * sin\(theta\)\) / g.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Maximum Height \(H\):) Tj
T*
(   At the apex, vertical velocity vy = 0: 0 = u*sin\(theta\) - g*t_apex => t_apex = \(u*sin\(theta\)\) /) Tj
T*
