(   - Kinetic friction opposing motion: F_k = mu_k * N_A = 0.25 * 392.4 = 98.10 N \(directed left\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cable tension T \(directed right\).) Tj
T*
(   - D'Alembert inertia force: F_inertia_A = m_A * a = 40 * a \(directed left, opposing motion\).) Tj
T*
(   Dynamic equilibrium equation \(Sigma F_x = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   T - F_k - m_A * a = 0 => T - 98.10 - 40 * a = 0 => T = 40 * a + 98.10. \(Equation 1\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Dynamic Equilibrium of Block B \(Hanging Vertically\):) Tj
T*
(   Forces acting on B:) Tj
T*
(   - Gravity weight: W_B = m_B * g = 25 * 9.81 = 245.25 N \(downward\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cable tension T \(upward\).) Tj
T*
(   - D'Alembert inertia force: F_inertia_B = m_B * a = 25 * a \(upward, opposing downward) Tj
T*
(   acceleration\).) Tj
T*
(   Dynamic equilibrium equation \(Sigma F_y = 0, downward positive\):) Tj
T*
(   W_B - T - m_B * a = 0 => 245.25 - T - 25 * a = 0 => T = 245.25 - 25 * a. \(Equation 2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Solve System Equations:) Tj
T*
(   Equating Equation 1 and Equation 2:) Tj
T*
(   40 * a + 98.10 = 245.25 - 25 * a => 65 * a = 147.15.) Tj
T*
(   a = 147.15 / 65 = 2.2638 m/s^2 =~ 2.26 m/s^2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Calculate Cable Tension T:) Tj
T*
(   Substitute a into Eq 1: T = 40 * \(2.2638\) + 98.10 = 90.55 + 98.10 = 188.65 N.) Tj
T*
(   Verify with Eq 2: T = 245.25 - 25 * \(2.2638\) = 245.25 - 56.60 = 188.65 N. \(Exact match!\)) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion: System acceleration a = 2.26 m/s^2; Cable tension T = 188.65 N.) Tj
