BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the Work-Energy Theorem for a particle undergoing rectilinear translation subjected to a resultant force F\(s\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Differential Form:) Tj
T*
(   By Newton's Second Law: F = m * a.) Tj
T*
(   Using the kinematic differential relation a = v * \(dv/ds\):) Tj
T*
(   F = m * v * \(dv/ds\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Separation of Variables:) Tj
T*
(   Multiplying both sides by differential displacement ds:) Tj
T*
(   F ds = m * v dv.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Definite Integration Over State Transition \(1 to 2\):) Tj
T*
(   Integrate the left side from initial position s1 to final position s2, and right side from) Tj
T*
(   initial velocity v1 to v2:) Tj
T*
(   Integral_s1^s2 F ds = Integral_v1^v2 m * v dv.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Evaluation of Integrals:) Tj
T*
(   The left side is by definition the Total Work Done U_1-2 by the resultant force:) Tj
T*
(   U_1-2 = Integral_s1^s2 F ds.) Tj
T*
(   The right side integrates directly:) Tj
T*
(   Integral_v1^v2 m * v dv = m * [ 0.5 * v^2 ]_v1^v2 = 0.5 * m * v2^2 - 0.5 * m * v1^2 = KE_2 -) Tj
T*
(   KE_1 = Delta KE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Theorem Statement:) Tj
T*
(   U_1-2 = KE_2 - KE_1 = Delta KE.) Tj
T*
(   'The total work performed by all external active and reactive forces on a particle equals the) Tj
T*
