/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Distinguish between Conservative and Non-Conservative forces in engineering mechanics. Derive the principle of Conservation of Mechanical Energy from the Work-Energy Theorem.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conservative Forces:) Tj
T*
(   A force F is conservative if the work it performs on a particle moving between two points) Tj
T*
(   depends ONLY on the initial and final endpoints,) Tj
T*
(   and is completely independent of the physical geometric path taken.) Tj
T*
(   - Mathematically: Closed path line integral is zero: Point_Integral F dot dr = 0; Curl of force) Tj
T*
(   field vanishes: Del x F = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - A scalar potential energy function V\(r\) exists such that: F = - Grad\(V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Work done: U_1-2 = - \(V_2 - V_1\) = - Delta V.) Tj
T*
(   - Classical Examples: Gravitational force \(V_g = m*g*y\), Linear spring force \(V_e = 0.5*k*x^2\),) Tj
T*
(   Electrostatic force.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Non-Conservative Forces:) Tj
T*
(   A force is non-conservative \(dissipative\) if the work done depends on the actual path length) Tj
T*
(   traversed.) Tj
T*
(   - Closed path integral is non-zero: Point_Integral F_nc dot dr != 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanical energy is irreversibly converted into thermal energy \(heat\), sound, or material) Tj
T*
(   plastic deformation.) Tj
T*
(   - Examples: Coulomb dry friction, aerodynamic fluid drag, viscous damping.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of Conservation of Mechanical Energy:) Tj
T*
(   Let total work be partitioned into conservative work U_cons and non-conservative work U_nc:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma U_1-2 = U_cons + U_nc = Delta KE = KE_2 - KE_1.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute U_cons = - \(V_2 - V_1\) = V_1 - V_2:) Tj
T*
(   \(V_1 - V_2\) + U_nc = KE_2 - KE_1.) Tj
T*
(   Rearranging terms:) Tj
T*
(   \(KE_1 + V_1\) + U_nc = KE_2 + V_2.) Tj
T*
(   If all acting forces are conservative \(U_nc = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   KE_1 + V_1 = KE_2 + V_2 = E_total = Constant.) Tj
T*
(   'In an isolated system governed solely by conservative forces, total mechanical energy \(KE +) Tj
T*
(   PE\) is strictly conserved.') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
