(   [Problem Statement]: A civil railway buffer stop consists of two parallel coil springs of stiffness k = 150 kN/m each. A runaway shunting rail wagon of mass m = 18,000 kg strikes the buffer with an initial speed of v0 = 2.5 m/s. Using energy conservation, calculate: \(1\) Maximum compression x_max of the buffer springs, \(2\) Maximum retarding force exerted on the wagon.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mechanical Energy Balance:) Tj
T*
(   Initial state \(at contact\): wagon speed v0 = 2.5 m/s, spring compression x = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Initial kinetic energy: KE_1 = 0.5 * m * v0^2 = 0.5 * 18000 * \(2.5\)^2 = 9000 * 6.25 = 56,250 J) Tj
T*
(   \(56.25 kJ\).) Tj
T*
(   Initial elastic potential energy: V_e1 = 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Peak Compression State:) Tj
T*
(   At maximum compression x_max, wagon comes instantaneously to rest: KE_2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Total equivalent spring stiffness of two parallel springs: k_eq = 2 * k = 2 * 150 = 300 kN/m =) Tj
T*
(   300,000 N/m.) Tj
T*
