(   [Problem Statement]: State the Principle of Linear Impulse and Momentum for a particle. Explain its derivation from Newton's Second Law and state under what physical conditions Linear Momentum is conserved.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Principle Statement:) Tj
T*
(   The linear impulse of the resultant external force acting on a particle over a time interval) Tj
T*
(   [t1, t2] is identically equal) Tj
T*
(   to the change in linear momentum of the particle over that same interval:) Tj
T*
(   Integral_t1^t2 Sigma F dt = m * v2 - m * v1 = Delta p.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   Newton's Second Law in momentum form:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma F = dp / dt = d/dt\( m * v \).) Tj
T*
(   For constant mass m: Sigma F dt = d\( m * v \).) Tj
T*
(   Integrating both sides between limits t1 and t2:) Tj
T*
(   Integral_t1^t2 Sigma F dt = Integral_v1^v2 d\( m * v \) = [ m * v ]_v1^v2 = m * v2 - m * v1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Conditions for Conservation of Linear Momentum:) Tj
T*
(   If the resultant external force acting on a system along a given direction axis \(say x-axis\) is) Tj
T*
(   ZERO \(Sigma F_x_ext = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Integral_t1^t2 \(Sigma F_x_ext\) dt = 0 => Delta p_x = 0 => \(p_x\)_total = constant.) Tj
T*
(   Sigma \(m_i * v_ix\)_initial = Sigma \(m_i * v_ix\)_final.) Tj
T*
(   Key Applications: Ballistic impact, explosive separation, jet propulsion, vehicle collisions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
