(   [Problem Statement]: Define the Coefficient of Restitution \(e\) for collision of two bodies. Classify the impact regimes based on values of e and derive the formula for loss of kinetic energy in direct central impact.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Physical Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   The Coefficient of Restitution 'e' is the negative ratio of relative velocity after impact to) Tj
T*
(   relative velocity before impact:) Tj
T*
(   e = - \(v_B2 - v_A2\) / \(v_B1 - v_A1\) = \(v_B2 - v_A2\) / \(v_A1 - v_B1\) = Relative Velocity of) Tj
T*
(   Separation / Relative Velocity of Approach.) Tj
T*
(   Physically, e is the ratio of restitution impulse \(recovery of deformation\) to deformation) Tj
T*
(   impulse during the collision contact phase:) Tj
T*
(   e = Integral\(R dt\) / Integral\(D dt\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Classification of Collision Regimes:) Tj
T*
(   - Perfectly Elastic Impact \(e = 1.0\): Total recovery of initial deformation. Mechanical kinetic) Tj
T*
(   energy is 100% conserved \(Delta KE = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inelastic / Semi-Elastic Impact \(0 < e < 1.0\): Partial plastic deformation and) Tj
T*
(   acoustic/thermal dissipation. Kinetic energy decreases.) Tj
T*
(   - Perfectly Plastic Impact \(e = 0.0\): Zero recovery; bodies coalesce and travel with identical) Tj
T*
(   common velocity \(v_A2 = v_B2\). Maximum possible KE loss.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Analytical Formula for Kinetic Energy Loss:) Tj
T*
(   Combining momentum conservation and restitution equation yields:) Tj
T*
(   Delta KE = KE_initial - KE_final = 0.5 * [ \(m1 * m2\) / \(m1 + m2\) ] * \(v_A1 - v_B1\)^2 * \(1 -) Tj
T*
(   e^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Observations:) Tj
T*
(   - If e = 1: 1 - e^2 = 0 => Delta KE = 0 \(perfect energy conservation\).) Tj
T*
(   - If e = 0: Delta KE = 0.5 * [ \(m1 * m2\) / \(m1 + m2\) ] * \(v_A1 - v_B1\)^2 \(maximum possible) Tj
T*
(   dissipation\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
