(   [Problem Statement]: A civil water tank overflow pipe discharges water horizontally from a height h = 20 m above ground at initial horizontal speed u = 12 m/s. Calculate: \(1\) Time taken for water stream to hit ground, \(2\) Horizontal distance x reached from pipe outlet, \(3\) Magnitude and angle of velocity at ground impact \(g = 9.81 m/s^2\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Time of Flight \(t_flight\):) Tj
T*
(   Horizontal projection implies initial vertical velocity u_y = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Vertical kinematics under gravity: h = 0.5 * g * t^2 => 20 = 0.5 * 9.81 * t^2 = 4.905 * t^2.) Tj
T*
(   t^2 = 20 / 4.905 = 4.0775 => t_flight = sqrt\(4.0775\) = 2.019 s =~ 2.02 seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Horizontal Distance \(x\):) Tj
T*
(   Horizontal motion is unaccelerated: a_x = 0.) Tj
T*
(   x = u * t_flight = 12.0 * 2.019 = 24.23 meters.) Tj
T*
