(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the kinematics of a particle moving in a plane using Polar Coordinates \(r, theta\). Derive the equations for radial velocity, transverse velocity, radial acceleration, and transverse acceleration.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Position Vector Representation:) Tj
T*
(   Let unit vectors be u_r \(directed radially outward along position vector r\) and u_theta) Tj
T*
(   \(perpendicular to u_r in direction of increasing theta\).) Tj
T*
(   Position vector: r = r * u_r.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Time Derivatives of Polar Unit Vectors:) Tj
T*
(   By geometric resolution in Cartesian frame:) Tj
T*
(   u_r = cos\(theta\) * i + sin\(theta\) * j.) Tj
T*
(   u_theta = - sin\(theta\) * i + cos\(theta\) * j.) Tj
T*
(   Differentiating with respect to time t:) Tj
T*
(   d\(u_r\)/dt = [ - sin\(theta\) * i + cos\(theta\) * j ] * \(dtheta/dt\) = theta_dot * u_theta.) Tj
T*
(   d\(u_theta\)/dt = [ - cos\(theta\) * i - sin\(theta\) * j ] * \(dtheta/dt\) = - theta_dot * u_r.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Velocity Vector in Polar Coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   v = dr/dt = d/dt\( r * u_r \) = \(dr/dt\) * u_r + r * \(du_r/dt\) = r_dot * u_r + r * theta_dot *) Tj
T*
(   u_theta.) Tj
T*
(   - Radial velocity: v_r = r_dot.) Tj
T*
(   - Transverse velocity: v_theta = r * theta_dot.) Tj
T*
(   - Total velocity magnitude: v = sqrt\( \(r_dot\)^2 + \(r * theta_dot\)^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Acceleration Vector in Polar Coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   a = dv/dt = d/dt\( r_dot * u_r + r * theta_dot * u_theta \).) Tj
T*
(   a = [ r_ddot * u_r + r_dot * \(theta_dot * u_theta\) ] + [ \(r_dot * theta_dot + r * theta_ddot\) *) Tj
T*
(   u_theta + r * theta_dot * \(- theta_dot * u_r\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Regrouping components along u_r and u_theta:) Tj
T*
(   a = [ r_ddot - r * \(theta_dot\)^2 ] * u_r + [ r * theta_ddot + 2 * r_dot * theta_dot ] *) Tj
T*
(   u_theta.) Tj
T*
(   - Radial Acceleration: a_r = r_ddot - r * \(theta_dot\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Transverse Acceleration: a_theta = r * theta_ddot + 2 * r_dot * theta_dot = \(1/r\) * d/dt\( r^2) Tj
T*
(   * theta_dot \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
