BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the civil engineering concept of Highway Superelevation \(Banking of Roads\). Derive the design relationship for equilibrium banking angle theta in terms of design speed v, curve radius R, and acceleration due to gravity g.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Background:) Tj
T*
(   When a vehicle negotiates a horizontal curve of radius R at speed v, it experiences a) Tj
T*
(   centripetal acceleration a_n = v^2 / R.) Tj
T*
(   If the road is completely flat, the required inward centripetal force must be supplied solely) Tj
T*
(   by lateral tyre-pavement friction:) Tj
T*
(   F_friction = m * v^2 / R <= mu_s * m * g => v_max = sqrt\( mu_s * g * R \).) Tj
T*
(   To eliminate reliance on lateral friction and prevent vehicle rollover or skidding on wet/icy) Tj
T*
(   roads, the outer edge of the pavement is elevated) Tj
T*
(   above the inner edge by angle theta, termed Superelevation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Dynamic Equilibrium Analysis \(No Lateral Friction Required\):) Tj
T*
(   Let the vehicle mass be m. The only forces acting are:) Tj
T*
(   - Gravity weight: W = m * g \(acting vertically downward\).) Tj
T*
(   - Pavement normal reaction: N \(acting perpendicular to banked road surface at angle theta to) Tj
T*
(   vertical\).) Tj
T*
(   Resolving forces in vertical and horizontal directions:) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical Equilibrium \(no vertical acceleration\): N * cos\(theta\) - m * g = 0 => N * cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   = m * g. \(Eq 1\)) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal Kinetics \(supplying centripetal acceleration a_n = v^2 / R\):) Tj
T*
(   N * sin\(theta\) = m * a_n = m * \(v^2 / R\). \(Eq 2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of Equilibrium Superelevation Formula:) Tj
T*
(   Dividing Eq 2 by Eq 1:) Tj
T*
(   [ N * sin\(theta\) ] / [ N * cos\(theta\) ] = [ m * \(v^2 / R\) ] / [ m * g ].) Tj
T*
(   tan\(theta\) = v^2 / \(g * R\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
