(>> Solution to Question 19:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A civil highway curve of radius R = 200 m has a design speed limit of v = 72 km/h \(20 m/s\). \(1\) Determine the required equilibrium banking angle theta. \(2\) If a vehicle navigates the banked curve at v = 90 km/h \(25 m/s\), compute the minimum coefficient of static friction mu_s needed to prevent outward skidding \(g = 9.81 m/s^2\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Design Banking Angle theta \(No Friction at 20 m/s\):) Tj
T*
(   tan\(theta\) = v^2 / \(g * R\) = \(20\)^2 / \(9.81 * 200\) = 400 / 1962 = 0.20387.) Tj
T*
(   theta = atan\(0.20387\) = 11.52 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   cos\(11.52 deg\) = 0.9798; sin\(11.52 deg\) = 0.1997.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Vehicle at Higher Speed v = 25 m/s \(Impeding Outward Skid\):) Tj
T*
(   At v = 25 m/s, required centripetal acceleration a_n = \(25\)^2 / 200 = 625 / 200 = 3.125 m/s^2.) Tj
T*
(   Tyre friction force F_s acts INWARD down the incline \(opposing outward skid\).) Tj
T*
(   Resolving parallel and perpendicular to the banked incline:) Tj
T*
(   - Normal to incline:) Tj
T*
(   N = m * g * cos\(theta\) + m * \(v^2 / R\) * sin\(theta\) = m * [ 9.81 * 0.9798 + 3.125 * 0.1997 ] =) Tj
T*
(   m * [ 9.612 + 0.624 ] = 10.236 * m.) Tj
T*
(   - Parallel to incline \(inward down the plane\):) Tj
T*
(   F_s + m * g * sin\(theta\) = m * \(v^2 / R\) * cos\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   F_s = m * [ 3.125 * 0.9798 - 9.81 * 0.1997 ] = m * [ 3.062 - 1.959 ] = 1.103 * m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Minimum Coefficient of Static Friction mu_s:) Tj
T*
(   mu_s = F_s / N = \(1.103 * m\) / \(10.236 * m\) = 0.1077 =~ 0.11.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion: Equilibrium banking angle = 11.52 degrees; Minimum friction required at 90 km/h is) Tj
T*
(   mu_s = 0.11.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
