(>> Solution to Question 20:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A continuous conveyor belt in a civil aggregates plant elevates gravel at mass flow rate dm/dt = 40 kg/s through vertical height h = 12 m at constant speed v = 2.5 m/s. Calculate: \(1\) Gravitational power required to elevate the gravel, \(2\) Kinematic power required to accelerate gravel from rest onto the belt, \(3\) Total minimum electric motor power needed assuming 85% mechanical transmission efficiency.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Gravitational Elevating Power \(P_gravity\):) Tj
T*
(   Work done against gravity per unit time:) Tj
T*
(   P_gravity = \(dm/dt\) * g * h = 40 kg/s * 9.81 m/s^2 * 12 m = 4708.8 W = 4.709 kW.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Kinematic Acceleration Power \(P_kinetic\):) Tj
T*
(   Gravel dropped vertically from rest onto the horizontal belt must be accelerated to belt speed) Tj
T*
(   v = 2.5 m/s.) Tj
T*
(   By momentum rate of change: F_traction = \(dm/dt\) * v = 40 * 2.5 = 100 N.) Tj
T*
(   Power expended by belt drive: P_belt = F_traction * v = \(dm/dt\) * v^2 = 40 * \(2.5\)^2 = 40 *) Tj
T*
(   6.25 = 250 W = 0.25 kW.) Tj
T*
(   \(Note: Half of this power is kinetic energy gained, half is dissipated in initial slip) Tj
T*
(   friction\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Total Net Mechanical Power:) Tj
T*
(   P_net = P_gravity + P_belt = 4708.8 + 250.0 = 4958.8 W = 4.959 kW.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Total Electric Motor Power \(Accounting for 85% Efficiency\):) Tj
T*
(   eta = 0.85.) Tj
T*
(   P_motor = P_net / eta = 4.959 kW / 0.85 = 5.834 kW =~ 5.83 kW.) Tj
T*
ET

