BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the direct central impact of two bodies A and B with masses m_A and m_B travelling with initial collinear velocities v_A1 and v_B1. Derive explicit formulas for post-impact velocities v_A2 and v_B2 in terms of coefficient of restitution 'e'.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Governing Conservation Principles:) Tj
T*
(   - Conservation of Linear Momentum along line of impact:) Tj
T*
(   m_A * v_A1 + m_B * v_B1 = m_A * v_A2 + m_B * v_B2. \(Equation 1\)) Tj
T*
(   - Coefficient of Restitution definition:) Tj
T*
(   e = \(v_B2 - v_A2\) / \(v_A1 - v_B1\) => v_B2 - v_A2 = e * \(v_A1 - v_B1\). \(Equation 2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of v_A2 \(Post-Impact Velocity of Body A\):) Tj
T*
(   From Equation 2: v_B2 = v_A2 + e * \(v_A1 - v_B1\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute into Equation 1:) Tj
T*
(   m_A * v_A1 + m_B * v_B1 = m_A * v_A2 + m_B * [ v_A2 + e * \(v_A1 - v_B1\) ].) Tj
T*
(   m_A * v_A1 + m_B * v_B1 = \(m_A + m_B\) * v_A2 + m_B * e * \(v_A1 - v_B1\).) Tj
T*
(   \(m_A + m_B\) * v_A2 = m_A * v_A1 + m_B * v_B1 - m_B * e * \(v_A1 - v_B1\).) Tj
T*
(   v_A2 = [ \(m_A - e * m_B\) * v_A1 + m_B * \(1 + e\) * v_B1 ] / \(m_A + m_B\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of v_B2 \(Post-Impact Velocity of Body B\):) Tj
T*
(   Similarly, isolating v_A2 = v_B2 - e * \(v_A1 - v_B1\) and substituting into Equation 1 yields:) Tj
T*
(   v_B2 = [ m_A * \(1 + e\) * v_A1 + \(m_B - e * m_A\) * v_B1 ] / \(m_A + m_B\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Special Verification Cases:) Tj
T*
(   - Elastic equal masses \(m_A = m_B, e = 1\): v_A2 = v_B1 and v_B2 = v_A1 \(velocities perfectly) Tj
T*
(   interchange!\).) Tj
T*
(   - Perfectly plastic \(e = 0\): v_A2 = v_B2 = \(m_A*v_A1 + m_B*v_B1\) / \(m_A + m_B\) \(common unified) Tj
T*
(   velocity\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 24:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A civil railway wagon A of mass m_A = 30 tonnes moves at v_A1 = 4.0 m/s and collides with stationary wagon B of mass m_B = 20 tonnes \(v_B1 = 0\). If the coefficient of restitution of the spring couplers is e = 0.60, calculate: \(1\) Velocities v_A2 and v_B2 after impact, \(2\) Total initial and final kinetic energies, \(3\) Percentage kinetic energy loss.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Post-Impact Velocities:) Tj
T*
(   Total mass M = m_A + m_B = 30 + 20 = 50 tonnes.) Tj
T*
(   Using derived impact formulas:) Tj
T*
(   v_A2 = [ \(m_A - e * m_B\) * v_A1 + m_B * \(1 + e\) * v_B1 ] / M.) Tj
T*
(   v_A2 = [ \(30 - 0.60 * 20\) * 4.0 + 0 ] / 50 = [ \(30 - 12\) * 4.0 ] / 50 = [ 18 * 4.0 ] / 50 = 72) Tj
T*
(   / 50 = 1.44 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   v_B2 = [ m_A * \(1 + e\) * v_A1 + \(m_B - e * m_A\) * v_B1 ] / M.) Tj
T*
(   v_B2 = [ 30 * \(1 + 0.60\) * 4.0 + 0 ] / 50 = [ 30 * 1.60 * 4.0 ] / 50 = 192 / 50 = 3.84 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Check Relative Velocity Separation:) Tj
T*
(   v_B2 - v_A2 = 3.84 - 1.44 = 2.40 m/s.) Tj
T*
(   e * \(v_A1 - v_B1\) = 0.60 * \(4.0 - 0\) = 2.40 m/s. \(Exact restitution match!\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Kinetic Energy Balance:) Tj
T*
(   - Initial KE: KE_1 = 0.5 * 30,000 * \(4.0\)^2 = 15,000 * 16 = 240,000 J \(240.0 kJ\).) Tj
T*
(   - Final KE: KE_2 = 0.5 * 30,000 * \(1.44\)^2 + 0.5 * 20,000 * \(3.84\)^2) Tj
T*
(   KE_2 = 15,000 * 2.0736 + 10,000 * 14.7456 = 31,104 + 147,456 = 178,560 J \(178.56 kJ\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Energy Dissipated:) Tj
T*
ET

