ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the mechanics of Oblique Central Impact between two smooth spherical particles. Detail the resolution along the Line of Impact \(common normal\) and the Plane of Contact \(common tangent\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometric Decomposition:) Tj
T*
(   Let the common normal passing through the centers of both spherical bodies at the instant of) Tj
T*
(   contact be designated the n-axis \(Line of Impact\).) Tj
T*
(   Let the orthogonal line tangent to both smooth surfaces be designated the t-axis \(Plane of) Tj
T*
(   Contact\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Tangential Axis Behavior \(t-axis\):) Tj
T*
(   Because both bodies are smooth, the contact forces during impact are strictly normal) Tj
T*
(   \(frictionless contact, F_tangential = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, NO impulse acts along the tangential t-direction on either particle:) Tj
T*
(   v_At2 = v_At1, and v_Bt2 = v_Bt1.) Tj
T*
(   'The velocity component of each individual body parallel to the plane of contact remains) Tj
T*
(   strictly invariant throughout the collision.') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Normal Axis Behavior \(n-axis\):) Tj
T*
(   All contact impulses act along the normal n-axis \(line of impact\).) Tj
T*
(   Along the n-axis, the collision is governed by standard direct central impact relations:) Tj
T*
(   - Conservation of Total Normal Momentum: m_A * v_An1 + m_B * v_Bn1 = m_A * v_An2 + m_B * v_Bn2.) Tj
T*
(   - Coefficient of Restitution along n-axis: e = \(v_Bn2 - v_An2\) / \(v_An1 - v_Bn1\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Resultant Post-Impact Velocities:) Tj
T*
(   Once normal components \(v_An2, v_Bn2\) are computed, the final velocity vectors are) Tj
T*
(   reconstructed:) Tj
T*
(   v_A2 = sqrt\( v_An2^2 + v_At2^2 \), at angle theta_A2 = atan\( v_At2 / v_An2 \).) Tj
T*
(   v_B2 = sqrt\( v_Bn2^2 + v_Bt2^2 \), at angle theta_B2 = atan\( v_Bt2 / v_Bn2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
