(   [Problem Statement]: A 200 g tennis ball strikes a rigid concrete foundation slab at angle theta1 = 45 degrees to the surface normal with speed v1 = 20 m/s. If the coefficient of restitution between ball and slab is e = 0.70 \(smooth slab\), compute: \(1\) Rebound velocity v2 magnitude, \(2\) Rebound angle theta2 with the normal, \(3\) Linear impulse exerted by the slab.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Velocity Decomposition Along Normal \(n\) and Tangential \(t\) Axes:) Tj
T*
(   - Normal component before impact: v_n1 = v1 * cos\(45\) = 20 * 0.7071 = 14.142 m/s \(toward slab\).) Tj
T*
(   - Tangential component before impact: v_t1 = v1 * sin\(45\) = 20 * 0.7071 = 14.142 m/s \(parallel) Tj
T*
(   to slab\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Post-Impact Components \(Rigid Slab mass -> infinity, v_slab = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   - Tangential component \(frictionless surface\): v_t2 = v_t1 = 14.142 m/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Normal component: v_n2 = e * v_n1 = 0.70 * 14.142 = 9.8995 m/s \(rebounding away from slab\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Rebound Speed and Angle:) Tj
T*
(   - Rebound speed: v2 = sqrt\( v_t2^2 + v_n2^2 \) = sqrt\( \(14.142\)^2 + \(9.8995\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 200.0 +) Tj
T*
(   98.0 \) = sqrt\( 298.0 \) = 17.26 m/s.) Tj
T*
ET

