(>> Solution to Question 28:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive Tsiolkovsky's Rocket Equation for variable mass systems moving in free space without external gravity. Explain how Newton's Second Law is extended to systems with continuously changing mass.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Variable Mass System Dynamics:) Tj
T*
(   Consider a system \(rocket\) of mass m at time t moving with velocity v. Total momentum: p\(t\) = m) Tj
T*
(   * v.) Tj
T*
(   Over time dt, an infinitesimal fuel mass dm is ejected backward with exhaust velocity u_e) Tj
T*
(   relative to the rocket.) Tj
T*
(   Absolute velocity of ejected mass in inertial frame: v_exhaust = v - u_e.) Tj
T*
(   The rocket's new mass is \(m - dm\) and its new velocity is \(v + dv\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Momentum Balance at time t + dt:) Tj
T*
(   p\(t + dt\) = \(m - dm\) * \(v + dv\) + dm * \(v - u_e\).) Tj
T*
(   p\(t + dt\) = m*v + m*dv - v*dm - dm*dv + v*dm - u_e*dm.) Tj
T*
(   Neglecting higher-order differential product dm*dv:) Tj
T*
(   p\(t + dt\) = m*v + m*dv - u_e*dm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Equating Impulse to Momentum Change:) Tj
T*
(   With zero external forces \(Sigma F_ext = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   dp = p\(t + dt\) - p\(t\) = 0 => m * dv - u_e * dm = 0 => m * dv = u_e * dm.) Tj
T*
(   Recognizing that dm is the decrease in rocket mass \(dm = - d\(m_rocket\)\):) Tj
T*
ET

