/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A civil engineering cable car of mass M = 1500 kg is pulled up a 20-degree incline track by a winch cable. The winch motor applies a tractive force P\(s\) = \(8000 + 400*s - 10*s^2\) N, where s is distance along the track in meters. Track rolling resistance is constant at F_r = 1200 N. Using the Work-Energy Principle, determine the velocity of the car after it traverses s = 30 m starting from rest at s = 0 \(g = 9.81 m/s^2\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Forces Acting Parallel to Incline Track:) Tj
T*
(   - Winch driving force: P\(s\) = 8000 + 400*s - 10*s^2 N.) Tj
T*
(   - Component of gravity opposing motion: W_parallel = M * g * sin\(20\) = 1500 * 9.81 * 0.34202 =) Tj
T*
(   5032.8 N.) Tj
T*
(   - Rolling resistance opposing motion: F_r = 1200.0 N.) Tj
T*
(   - Net driving force function:) Tj
T*
(   F_net\(s\) = P\(s\) - W_parallel - F_r = \(8000 + 400*s - 10*s^2\) - 5032.8 - 1200.0 = 1767.2 + 400*s) Tj
T*
(   - 10*s^2 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Total Work Performed Over Distance s = 30 m:) Tj
T*
(   U_1-2 = Integral_0^30 F_net\(s\) ds = Integral_0^30 \(1767.2 + 400*s - 10*s^2\) ds.) Tj
T*
(   U_1-2 = [ 1767.2 * s + 200 * s^2 - \(10/3\) * s^3 ]_0^30.) Tj
T*
(   - First term: 1767.2 * 30 = 53,016 J.) Tj
T*
(   - Second term: 200 * \(30\)^2 = 200 * 900 = 180,000 J.) Tj
T*
(   - Third term: \(10/3\) * \(27,000\) = 90,000 J.) Tj
T*
(   U_1-2 = 53,016 + 180,000 - 90,000 = 143,016 Joules \(143.02 kJ\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Calculate Final Velocity via Work-Energy Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   U_1-2 = KE_2 - KE_1 = 0.5 * M * v^2 - 0.) Tj
T*
(   143,016 = 0.5 * 1500 * v^2 = 750 * v^2.) Tj
T*
(   v^2 = 143,016 / 750 = 190.688 \(m/s\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   v = sqrt\(190.688\) = 13.809 m/s =~ 13.81 m/s \(49.7 km/h\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion: Final cable car velocity at 30 m is v = 13.81 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
