(   - Method 3: Impulse-Momentum Principle:) Tj
T*
(   * Governing equation: Integral_t1^t2 Sigma F dt = m * v2 - m * v1 = Delta p.) Tj
T*
(   * Vector formulation: Integrates forces over elapsed TIME interval dt.) Tj
T*
(   * Ideal for transient high-magnitude forces \(impact, explosions, pile-driving\) where contact) Tj
T*
(   time dt -> 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Engineering Decision Matrix / Selection Strategy:) Tj
T*
(   - Select Work-Energy when variables involve Force, Distance \(Displacement\), and Velocity \(F, s,) Tj
T*
(   v\), and time 't' is neither given nor required.) Tj
T*
(   - Select Impulse-Momentum when variables involve Force, Time, and Velocity \(F, t, v\), or when) Tj
T*
(   solving collisions and impact events.) Tj
T*
(   - Select Newton's Second Law / D'Alembert when normal forces, friction limits, instantaneous) Tj
T*
(   cable tensions, or accelerations \(a\) are explicitly sought.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
